// Lab-only presentation entries, read by crates/client/tests/support/effect_subjects.rs.
//
// The effect review gates of plan docs/plans/2026-11-09-effect-visualization.md accepted the
// slice's `shell_impact`, `acid_burst` and `spine_line` (round 5, Amendment 3) and the
// scale-out's `flak_burst`, `flame_line`, `lance_sweep` and `cleave_impact` (scale-out rounds 1
// to 5, Amendment 9), so their presentation blocks live in assets/catalog/units.ron alone. What
// remains here is the one effect no shipped unit can use yet: `burrow_trail`, the trail of a
// burrowed unit moving underground (plan Amendment 2, R5). The shipped burrowed mode cannot
// move, so only the tests drive this unit with a velocity. Each entry gives a shipped unit (by
// slug) presentation entries that are added to its shipped block, so the lab binds the effect
// to that unit's real data.
//
// This is test data, not Rust, so it stays outside the zero-hardcoded-identities rule (charter
// §3.3). An entry here must not repeat a weapon or mode entry of the unit's shipped block, and
// an effect named here must not also be named by a shipped unit: the catalog test fails then,
// and the entry belongs in `units.ron` alone.
{
    "burrow_scorpion": (
        modes: [(mode: "burrowed", moving: Some("burrow_trail"))],
    ),
}
